# Example upssched.conf for RP-node2 (see CLAUDE.md topology).
#
# Install at /etc/nut/upssched.conf and adjust the CMDSCRIPT path to the
# real deploy path (CLAUDE.md: /home/pi/Projects/homelab-energy). This is a
# template only: nothing here is applied automatically, and it is not a
# substitute for upsmon.conf already having
#   NOTIFYCMD /usr/sbin/upssched
# and NOTIFYFLAG entries with the EXEC bit for the events below, e.g.:
#   NOTIFYFLAG ONLINE  SYSLOG+EXEC
#   NOTIFYFLAG ONBATT  SYSLOG+EXEC
#   NOTIFYFLAG LOWBATT SYSLOG+EXEC
#
# NOTIFYCMD points at upssched directly, not the upssched-cmd wrapper
# (NUT's documented norm). On RP-node2 (NUT 2.8.1), upssched-cmd's
# daemon/pipe forwarding (meant for START-TIMER/CANCEL-TIMER) silently did
# nothing — no log output, no CMDSCRIPT call, no error. Calling upssched
# directly worked immediately, and this config only uses immediate
# EXECUTE (no timers), so the daemon/pipe layer buys nothing here anyway.
# upsmon sets the UPSNAME/NOTIFYTYPE env vars upssched needs; it takes no
# CLI arguments. See CLAUDE.md's "Comportamiento de NUT ya medido" for
# this finding. PIPEFN/LOCKFN below are kept because upssched requires
# them to be set even when nothing uses the pipe.
#
# upsmon runs upssched as its own notify user (e.g. "nut", split from
# the root process that does the actual shutdown), not whoever owns this
# checkout. bin/homelab-energy-cmdscript pins STATE_DIR to
# /var/lib/homelab-energy for that reason — see docs/runbook.md's
# pre-test checklist for creating that directory with the right owner.
# That same user also needs: execute (not necessarily read) access all
# the way down to bin/homelab-energy-cmdscript (a restrictive home
# directory like `chmod 700 ~pi` blocks this even if every subdirectory
# below it is otherwise world-readable — grant the notify user's group
# execute-only access on the home directory itself), and ownership of
# /etc/homelab-energy/secrets.env (config.sh refuses to load a secrets
# file that's readable by any other user, including the checkout's own
# owner).

CMDSCRIPT /home/pi/Projects/homelab-energy/bin/homelab-energy-cmdscript

PIPEFN /var/run/nut/upssched.pipe
LOCKFN /var/run/nut/upssched.lock

AT ONBATT * EXECUTE ONBATT
AT ONLINE * EXECUTE ONLINE
AT LOWBATT * EXECUTE LOWBATT
